      "description": "RFC 8785 Section 3.2.3 orders member names by UTF-16 code unit. U+1F600 encodes as the surrogate pair D83D DE00, so it sorts BEFORE U+FF20 even though its code point is larger. A canonicalizer that sorts by code point (Python sorted / json.dumps(sort_keys=True), Rust and Go byte order) emits the other order and is non-conformant.",
